libfacts (2.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * C++: a program linked with the C library (libfacts, or facts.c alone)
    no longer aborts at its first fiction. Each C++ group now catches the
    fiction FACT throws; 2.4.0 caught it only in the C++ library.
  * MOVING-CC.md: a guide to moving hand-built C++ tests to facts.

 -- Warren MacEvoy <wmacevoy@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

libfacts (2.4.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * C++: FACT leaves its group by exception, so a fiction in a helper, method,
    or lambda ends the group, and a helper that returns a value can use FACT.
    FACT_BY_RETURN keeps the old way; FACT_BY_EXCEPTION names the new one.
    A build without exceptions leaves by return.
  * C++: a fiction shows a value of any type: its operator<<, a container's
    first 20 elements, a pair, or "?". Every comparison compiles.
  * C++: a class constant never defined outside its class links in a fact.
  * FactsCurrent() gives the group being run, so a helper with no Facts
    parameter can check facts.

 -- Warren MacEvoy <wmacevoy@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

libfacts (2.3.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * C++: facts::interval and facts::pm, so FACT(x == y + facts::pm(1e-9))
    states a tolerance; a fiction prints the value and the interval.
  * Safe execution no longer waits a second per run: the parent sleeps until
    the child ends or the timeout rings.
  * Stopping the supervising process (SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP) also stops the
    run it started.
  * --facts_include and --facts_exclude apply to what --facts_find registered,
    in either order.
  * Windows: a crash in a group is reported and exits 2.
  * The VS Code extension is deprecated.

 -- Warren MacEvoy <wmacevoy@gmail.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

libfacts (2.2.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * A run that checks no FACT is an error: exit code 2, not 0.
  * Arguments beginning --fact are reserved; an unknown one is an error and
    nothing runs. Other arguments are left to the program.
  * --facts_timeout refuses anything but a positive number of seconds.
  * New symbol: FactsMainIf, used by FACTS_MAIN_IF. A program using that
    macro must be rebuilt with this facts.h to link this library.

 -- Warren MacEvoy <wmacevoy@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

libfacts (2.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * C++: FACT(a op b) writes the comparison directly and still prints both
    values; FACT(a op b, note) adds a footnote built only for a fiction.
  * FACT(a,op,b) evaluates each side once in C with gcc or clang and in C++;
    elsewhere the console report warns when a run evaluated twice.
    New symbol: facts_twice.
  * The printed gdb hint runs with --facts_unsafe, so its breakpoints are
    reached under safe execution.
  * FACTS_TRACE and FACTS_WATCH build without warnings under -Wall -Wextra.
  * The console and JUnit reports are separated from the run; output is
    unchanged apart from the gdb hint.

 -- Warren MacEvoy <wmacevoy@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

libfacts (2.0.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Safe execution: fork/exec wrapper with crash detection, timeout, niceness.
  * Runtime test registration via --facts_find (dlsym-based).
  * --facts_register_all to print FACTS_REGISTER_ALL block.
  * Removed auto-discovery (memory scanning). Explicit registration required.
  * New CLI options: --facts_unsafe, --facts_timeout=N.

 -- Warren MacEvoy <wmacevoy@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
